      "id": "md2025_1559",
      "subset": "S4",
      "task_type": "cross-company",
      "question": "What differences exist between AEP and ED regarding their forward-looking statement disclaimers?",
      "expected_answer": "AEP's disclaimer includes an explicit list of factors that could cause actual results to differ, such as 'Changes in economic conditions, electric market demand and demographic patterns,' 'Inflationary or deflationary interest rate trends,' and 'New legislation.' ED's disclaimer is less enumerated; it states that strategies may not be effective to address changes in the external business environment and lists factors like 'Changes to the competitive landscape, public policy, laws or regulations (or interpretations thereof), customer behavior or technology.' Thus, AEP provides a more detailed enumerated list of risk factors.",
      "predicted_answer": "AEP's forward-looking statement disclaimer is explicitly presented in Item 7, identifying predictive words like \"expect,\" \"anticipate,\" \"intend,\" \"plan,\" \"believe,\" \"will,\" \"should,\" \"could,\" \"would,\" \"project,\" \"continue\" and similar expressions, and includes a non-exhaustive bulleted list of risk factors such as economic conditions, global conflicts, interest rates, and state legislation [E1][E3]. ED's retrieved Item 7 content does not contain a forward-looking statement disclaimer; instead, it discusses strategic risks under the heading \"The Companies' Strategies May Not Be Effective To Address Changes In The External Business Environment,\" covering competitive landscape changes, distributed energy resources, and climate policy impacts without any predictive language disclaimer or safe-harbor statement [E2]. The key difference is that AEP provides a formal forward-looking statement disclaimer with defined terminology and risk factors, while ED's scoped Item 7 evidence contains only operational risk discussion without such a disclaimer.\n\nSources:\n[E1] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E2] ED_2024.html — Item 7. The Companies' Strategies May Not Be Effective To Address Changes In The External Business Environment\n[E3] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations",
